# Temporary Scripts

When creating one-off, exploratory, or debugging scripts, write them to `packages/data/scripts/temp/` instead of `packages/data/scripts/`. The `packages/data/scripts/temp/` directory is gitignored and will not be committed.

Only scripts that are meant to be long-lived and re-run regularly should live in `packages/data/scripts/` directly. Write them as **TypeScript** (`.ts`) so `pnpm --filter @repo/data type-check` covers them.

## Package commands (`pnpm --filter @repo/data …`)

| Command      | Orchestrator                            | Purpose                                                          |
| ------------ | --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `extract`    | `scripts/1-extract/index.ts`            | Raw JSON harvest → `cache/raw/` (pokeapi, TCG, wiki-lore)        |
| `refresh`    | `scripts/1-extract/extract-periodic.ts` | Weekly cron: pokeapi / TCG / wiki-lore (no images)               |
| `images`     | `scripts/2-images/index.ts`             | Sprites + artofpkm + backfill + Blob publish + local cleanup (~yearly) |
| `transform`  | `scripts/3-transform/index.ts`          | Raw → normalized v2 + apply Blob URLs (fast; no upload)          |
| `enrich`     | `scripts/enrich/index.ts`               | Legacy live-API enrich (`cache/normalized/`)                     |
| `audit-tags` | `scripts/audit-collection-tags.ts`      | Read-only collection tag audit                                   |

### Typical workflows

**Weekly refresh (cron):**

```bash
pnpm --filter @repo/data refresh
pnpm --filter @repo/data transform
```

**New species / annual art refresh:**

```bash
pnpm --filter @repo/data extract    # if pokeapi raw needs update
pnpm --filter @repo/data images     # sprites, scene art, Blob upload
pnpm --filter @repo/data transform  # normalized JSON + URL patch
```

Both extract commands sync scratch repos automatically (clone or `git pull --ff-only`). Freshness is recorded in `cache/extract-manifest.json`.

PokeAPI bulk data uses the [PokeAPI/api-data](https://github.com/PokeAPI/api-data) git mirror — not [ditto clone](https://github.com/PokeAPI/ditto) (avoids Python tooling and live API rate limits). Live prices stay in `@repo/marketplaces` at runtime.

Run individual step files directly with `tsx scripts/…` when debugging a single step.

See `.cursor/rules/data-scripts-progress.mdc` for progress logging and fast blob skip requirements.

## Shared libs (`scripts/lib/`)

- `cache-paths.ts` — re-exports path constants from `src/paths.ts` (`speciesCacheDir`, `normalizedMetaDir`, etc.)
- `pokemon-cache.ts` — read/write `cache/normalized/species/{slug}.json` via `speciesCacheDir`
- `raw-pokeapi-index.ts` — list species from `cache/raw/pokeapi/` (extract layer; no normalized dependency)
- `argv.ts` — `--limit`, `--only`, flags
- `artofpkm-scraper.ts` — artofpkm.com scene art scrape
- `blob-manifest.ts` — idempotent Vercel Blob publish manifest
- `apply-blob-art.ts` — patch normalized species `art` from manifest

## Cache layout

Committed production enrich data lives under `packages/data/cache/normalized/`:

| Path                       | Contents                                                |
| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| `species/`                 | Per-species JSON + `index.json`                         |
| `meta/`                    | `ability-descriptions.json`, `pokemon-collections.json` |
| `cards/artists/`           | Artist TCG cache                                        |
| `cards/expensive-by-type/` | Per-type expensive card snapshots                       |
| `popularity/`              | Survey CSVs                                             |

Path constants are defined once in `packages/data/src/paths.ts`. Scripts should import from `./lib/cache-paths`, not hardcode paths.

Offline ETL: `1-extract` writes gitignored `raw/` and `scratch/` only (must not read `normalized/`). `2-images` writes `cache/images/` and `blob-manifest.json`. `3-transform` reads raw and writes normalized.
